# Broadcast Feature Upgrade Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Upgrade the Broadcast feature to match the "Pro" UI, enabling advanced targeting (Tags, Specific Users), real-time recipient counting, and support for Image messages. This involves full-stack updates from the database schema to the UI and background worker.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This upgrade involves a database schema change. A migration will be required.

## Proposed Changes

### Database ([prisma/schema.prisma](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/prisma/schema.prisma))
- Modify `BroadcastTarget` enum:
    - Add `TAG`
    - Add `SPECIFIC_USERS`
- Modify [Broadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#88-104) model:
    - Add `name` is already present. (Wait, checking schema...)
    - Schema has `name String`. Use this for "Broadcast Title".
    - `content` is [Json](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/broadcast/broadcast-form.tsx#83-93). Can hold image data.
    - `targetIds` is `String[]`. Can hold Tag IDs or User IDs.
    - **Wait, `targetConfig` was requested.**
    - User requested: `Add targetConfig (Json?)`.
    - Current schema has `targetIds String[]`.
    - If I use `targetIds`, it might be enough for `TAG` (list of tag names/ids) and `SPECIFIC_USERS` (list of user IDs).
    - `RICH_MENU` targeting uses `targetIds` currently ?
    - Let's check [run.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/workers/run.ts): `if (targetType === "RICH_MENU" && targetIds.length > 0) ... richMenuAliasId: { in: targetIds }`.
    - So `targetIds` works for a list of strings.
    - For `TAG`, we can store tag names in `targetIds`.
    - For `SPECIFIC_USERS`, we can store lineUserIds in `targetIds`.
    - **However**, the user explicitly asked for `targetConfig (Json?)`.
    - Reason: "To store details like `["tag_vip", "tag_new"]` or specific user IDs."
    - If `targetIds` (String[]) is already there, maybe `targetConfig` is redundant?
    - `targetIds` is `String[]`.
    - If we follow the user request strictly, we add `targetConfig`.
    - But `targetIds` is cleaner for simple arrays.
    - Let's look at `BroadcastLog` user mentioned.
    - Schema has [Broadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#88-104) model. It does not have `BroadcastLog`. I assume "BroadcastLog" meant the [Broadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#88-104) model which serves as a log/record.
    - User asked: `Add title (String?)`. Schema has `name String`. I will use `name`.
    - User asked: `Add targetConfig (Json?)`.
    - If I use `targetIds` for tags, it works.
    - I'll stick to `targetIds` if possible to avoid schema bloat, but if the user *really* wants `targetConfig` for future proofing (complex objects), I should consider it.
    - But `targetIds` is `String[]`.
    - I will **add `targetConfig`** as requested to be safe and strictly follow instructions, maybe they want to store more than just IDs (e.g. boolean logic).
    - Actually, `targetIds` is `String[]`. If we want to store `AND` vs `OR` logic for tags, we might need JSON.
    - I'll add `targetConfig` (Json) and `title` (Wait, `name` exists. I'll check if `name` is what they meant. "Broadcast Title" input -> `name`. I'll assume `name` is enough, but user said "Add title (String?)". I'll double check if I should rename or alias. The current `name` is used. I'll use `name` for "Broadcast Title").

### Server Actions
#### [src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts)
- **[NEW]** `calculateRecipientCount(targetType, targetConfig)`
    - Queries Prisma `count()` based on targeting.
    - Returns number of matching customers.
- **[MODIFY]** [sendBroadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#10-65)
    - Update signature to accept `targetConfig` (or map to it).
    - Support `messageType` check (Image vs Text vs Flex).

### UI Components
#### [src/components/broadcast/broadcast-form.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/broadcast/broadcast-form.tsx)
- **[MODIFY]** [BroadcastForm](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/broadcast/broadcast-form.tsx#45-421)
    - Top-level "Broadcast Name" input (maps to `name`).
    - Message Type Selection: Text, Image, Flex.
    - Image Input: URL input + Preview.
    - Targeting UI:
        - Grid/Card selection.
        - `TAG`: Multi-select from `Tag` model.
        - `SPECIFIC_USERS`: Text input (comma separated) or better UI? User said "Simple input for User ID (for now)".
    - Recipient Counter:
        - `useEffect` hook listening to `targetType` & config changes.
        - Calls `calculateRecipientCount`.
        - Displays count in blue bar.

### Worker
